WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:02.730
Something broke at three in the morning.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.380
Nobody noticed until nine.

3
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.565
Six hours of bad data.

4
00:00:06.585 --> 00:00:09.590
Build it so the pipeline tells you first.

5
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.525
Think of a car dashboard.

6
00:00:11.545 --> 00:00:13.775
Metrics are the gauges and warning lights.

7
00:00:13.795 --> 00:00:15.535
You set alerts on them.

8
00:00:15.555 --> 00:00:17.185
Logs are the mechanic's notes.

9
00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:19.270
They explain why it happened.

10
00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:24.680
Watch the Pub/Sub backlog, the oldest unacked message, and Dataflow's system lag.

11
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.615
A log sink sends matching logs somewhere else.

12
00:00:27.635 --> 00:00:29.490
To BigQuery for analysis.

13
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.465
To Cloud Storage for the archive.

14
00:00:31.485 --> 00:00:34.050
To Pub/Sub for an instant reaction.

15
00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:39.335
And for BigQuery itself, INFORMATION SCHEMA shows who ran what, and what it cost.

16
00:00:39.355 --> 00:00:43.410
The trap: polling the logs on a timer, when you need an instant alert.

17
00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.010
Use a sink to Pub/Sub.

18
00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:49.395
Second idea: the error message tells you the fix.

19
00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.933
A quota error means too many small requests.

20
00:00:51.953 --> 00:00:54.205
Batch them, or spread them out.

21
00:00:54.225 --> 00:00:57.565
For rate limits, retry with exponential backoff.

22
00:00:57.585 --> 00:01:00.503
Resources exceeded means one worker got too much.

23
00:01:00.523 --> 00:01:02.100
Rewrite the query.

24
00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.312
Permission denied?

25
00:01:03.332 --> 00:01:05.450
Check the identity that runs the job.

26
00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:08.775
It needs the data role, and job user.

27
00:01:08.795 --> 00:01:10.035
Recap.

28
00:01:10.055 --> 00:01:11.197
Metrics to alert.

29
00:01:11.217 --> 00:01:12.398
Logs to explain.

30
00:01:12.418 --> 00:01:13.895
Sinks to route.

31
00:01:13.915 --> 00:01:15.133
Quota means batch.

32
00:01:15.153 --> 00:01:17.220
Resources exceeded means rewrite.

33
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.705
Permission means check the identity.

34
00:01:19.725 --> 00:01:22.500
Try the checkpoint below.
